# bidezine-system — environment template
#
# Copy this file to `.env` on EACH machine and fill in the values. NEVER commit `.env`
# (it is gitignored). Secrets do not travel through git — set them per machine.

# Machine identity — used by HANDOFF.md's "one section per machine" protocol so an AI session
# can tell which section it's allowed to write to WITHOUT having to ask or guess. Set this once,
# per machine, to the exact section heading this machine owns in HANDOFF.md: "Laptop A", "Laptop B",
# or "PC". MACHINE_OWNER is just the human's name, for readability in logs/prompts.
MACHINE_NAME=
MACHINE_OWNER=

# Figma personal access token (used by the figma-developer-mcp server in .mcp.json)
FIGMA_API_KEY=

# ── Sandbox — Fabric SQL Database (docs/SANDBOX-SPEC.md, Milestone 1) ────────────────
# The Sandbox's operational store. Provisioned once in the Fabric portal, then every
# machine connects to the SAME database using its own service-principal credentials.
#
# FABRIC_SQL_SERVER   — server FQDN from the SQL database's Settings → Connection
#                       strings, ending in `.database.fabric.microsoft.com`. The
#                       database lives in the biDezine tenant; nothing in this project
#                       connects to any other tenant.
# FABRIC_SQL_DATABASE — the database name AS THE SERVER SEES IT. Fabric appends the
#                       item GUID, so this is not the short name you typed when
#                       creating it. Copy it verbatim.
# FABRIC_SQL_COLLATION— recorded for reference. SQL_Latin1_General_CP1_CI_AS is
#                       case-INSENSITIVE; any column needing case-sensitive comparison
#                       must declare an explicit COLLATE.
# FABRIC_TENANT_ID    — Entra ID (Azure AD) tenant/directory ID.
#
# FOUR service principals, not one. Fabric SQL authenticates through Entra ID rather
# than SQL logins, so each database role needs its own identity:
#   ADMIN  — runs schema migrations (db_owner; full DDL)
#   APP    — the Sandbox UI application
#   AGENT  — AI agents. DENIED insert on the evidence table. This deny is the core
#            invariant of the whole system (docs/SANDBOX-SPEC.md §3.4) — never grant
#            around it, never run agent work under a different principal.
#   RUNNER — the verification runner. The ONLY identity that may write evidence.
# Each *_CLIENT_SECRET is the secret VALUE, not its ID, and is shown only once.
FABRIC_SQL_SERVER=
FABRIC_SQL_DATABASE=
FABRIC_SQL_COLLATION=
FABRIC_TENANT_ID=
FABRIC_ADMIN_CLIENT_ID=
FABRIC_ADMIN_CLIENT_SECRET=
FABRIC_APP_CLIENT_ID=
FABRIC_APP_CLIENT_SECRET=
FABRIC_AGENT_CLIENT_ID=
FABRIC_AGENT_CLIENT_SECRET=
FABRIC_RUNNER_CLIENT_ID=
FABRIC_RUNNER_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Cloudflare — for deploying the verification site.
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
